    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **42 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented an optional, validated-when-present `postcode` field for owners.\n\n**What the change does**\n- Postcode is optional \u2014 an owner created without one is still accepted (backward-compatible contract).\n- When present, it must be exactly 4 digits, else **400**.\n- When present and the owner's city has a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), else **400**.\n- A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode.\n- The postcode is stored and returned when given.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so both `OwnerFieldsDto` input and `OwnerDto` output carry it; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` column, getter, and setter.\n- `function/owner/ValidatePostcode.java` (new) \u2014 validates when present (4-digit format + region range), throwing a checked `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- `escalation/InvalidPostcodeException.java` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` (new) \u2014 map the exception to a 400, mirroring the existing email/telephone handlers.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...InvalidPostcodeException.yml` (new) \u2014 wires the handler.\n- `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` \u2014 inserted the `validatePostcode` step after body validation.\n- `function/owner/ApplyOwner.java` \u2014 copies `postcode` on update (PUT).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column.\n\nThe validation reuses the existing `Localities.region(city)` table so the city\u2192region mapping stays a single source of truth.",
